Menu="Settings:50"
Title="Trove"
Icon="trove.png"
Type="menu"
---
<?php
// Trove settings (native Dynamix form). Writes the same cfg file the daemon
// reads; changes apply on next daemon settings reload.
$plugin = 'trove';
$cfg = parse_plugin_cfg($plugin);
if (!is_array($cfg)) {
    $cfg = [];
}
$dataDir = isset($cfg['DATA_DIR']) ? (string)$cfg['DATA_DIR'] : '';
$concurrency = isset($cfg['CONCURRENCY']) ? (string)$cfg['CONCURRENCY'] : '1';
$physicalWrite = isset($cfg['PHYSICAL_WRITE']) ? $cfg['PHYSICAL_WRITE'] : 'false';
$protectedMode = isset($cfg['PROTECTED_MODE']) ? (string)$cfg['PROTECTED_MODE'] : 'deny';
$expertMode = isset($cfg['EXPERT_MODE']) ? $cfg['EXPERT_MODE'] : 'false';
?>
<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="<?=$plugin?>/<?=$plugin?>.cfg">

_(Job data directory)_
: <input type="text" name="DATA_DIR" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($dataDir) ?>" placeholder="/mnt/user/trove-data" maxlength="256">

<blockquote class="inline_help">
Directory for the background job journal. It must live on the array or a pool
(under /mnt/...) — never on the USB flash boot device. Until this is set,
Trove runs in read-only mode and all write operations are disabled.
</blockquote>

_(Parallel jobs)_
: <select name="CONCURRENCY">
  <?=mk_option($concurrency, "1", "1")?>
  <?=mk_option($concurrency, "2", "2")?>
  <?=mk_option($concurrency, "3", "3")?>
  <?=mk_option($concurrency, "4", "4")?>
  </select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
Number of file operations that may run at the same time. The default of 1 is
deliberately conservative on spinning-disk arrays.
</blockquote>

_(System share write protection)_
: <select name="PROTECTED_MODE">
  <?=mk_option($protectedMode, "deny", _("Refuse writes (recommended)"))?>
  <?=mk_option($protectedMode, "ack", _("Require explicit confirmation"))?>
  </select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
appdata, domains, system and isos hold Docker/VM state. Writes into these
shares are refused by default; "require explicit confirmation" lets the file
manager proceed only after you acknowledge the warning in the app.
</blockquote>

_(Expert mode)_
: <select name="EXPERT_MODE">
  <?=mk_option($expertMode, "false", _("No"))?>
  <?=mk_option($expertMode, "true", _("Yes"))?>
  </select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
Show physical disks (/mnt/diskN) and pools (/mnt/&lt;pool&gt;) in the
navigation. Physical views are read-only unless physical writes are enabled
in the app settings; mixing them with logical shares in one operation is
always refused.
</blockquote>

<input type="submit" name="#default" value="_(Default)_">
: <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>
